            <ArticleTitle>[Computer-assisted reconstruction of coronary vessels].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>930-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>End stage coronary artery disease with linear stenosis of the main vessels despite several coronary interventions is a current challenge for surgical treatment. As the long term results are mainly determined by the pathology of the coronary vessels a simple revascularisation with arterial or venous grafts provides no adequate solution of the problem. An exactly controlled 3D-reconstruction of the coronary vessels enabling selective thrombendarteriectomy (TEA) seems to be a new approach, that may be limited by neointimal hyperproliferation of the coronary vessels. Intraoperative brachytherapy may be a tool to inhibit this process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
